<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43593" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδαιμον-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tending</i> or <i>conducive to happiness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1176b16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1367b13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ εὐ</span>. <i>the
				constituents thereof</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.2.34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελετὴ καλή τε καὶ εὐ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				253c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>likely to be happy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1134
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1099b3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ εὐ</span>. philosophers
				<i>who make happiness the chief good</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.17
			</span></i>; esp. of Anaxarchus, <i><span class="en">
				Clearch.
				14
			</span></i>; so also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. αἵρεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>Phil.Hist.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς, πράττειν,
				διάγειν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				856
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.2.9
			</span></i>.</div>
